cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PEACOCK, please cite this software release and the papers described on the citation page."
type: software
title: "PEACOCK: Profiles of Emission and Absorption from Clumpy Outflows with Complex Kinematics"
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Zhihui
    affiliation: "Johns Hopkins University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5113-7558"
  - family-names: Gronke
    given-names: Max
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2491-060X"
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
url: "https://peacock-rt.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/astro-lzh/PEACOCK"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  PEACOCK models ultraviolet emission and absorption in clumpy galactic winds
  with three-dimensional Monte Carlo radiative transfer, including resonance
  scattering, fluorescent re-emission in supported atomic networks and dust
  interactions. It provides CPU and CUDA transport with configurable cloud
  geometry and kinematics, and builds on Max Gronke's tlac framework.
